Description: read the node-monitor move destination as a virtual ref
 V\OS node-monitor messages do not carry the legacy integer fields:
 the destination arrives as the entry_ref named "virtual:to directory"
 (see kits/storage/PathMonitor.cpp, which sends exactly opcode + that
 ref + virtual:from directory + virtual:node). Upstream's
 FindInt32("device")/FindInt64("to directory") in EntryMoved therefore
 always fail silently on V\OS and the dock item keeps a stale ref after
 a file moves. FindRef on the sanctioned field name yields the whole
 entry_ref (device, new parent directory and name) in one call, so the
 manual set_name assembly goes away with it.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/8Dock

--- a/src/ItemView.cpp
+++ b/src/ItemView.cpp
@@ -406,13 +406,13 @@
 
 void CItemView::EntryMoved( BMessage *msg )
 {
-	const char *name;
-	
-	msg->FindInt32( "device", &mRef.device ); 
-	msg->FindInt64( "to directory", &mRef.directory );
-	msg->FindString( "name", &name );
-
-	mRef.set_name( name );
+	// V\OS node-monitor messages carry the move destination as a ref:
+	// "virtual:to directory" is the entry_ref (device, new parent
+	// directory, name) itself. The legacy integer device/directory
+	// fields such messages no longer carry always fail to read, so take
+	// the whole ref instead of assembling it from parts.
+	if (msg->FindRef( "virtual:to directory", &mRef ) != B_OK)
+		return;
 
 	BEntry e( &mRef );
 	e.GetPath( &mPath );
